Vendored build inputs for the Ubuntu PPA source package
========================================================

Launchpad's PPA builders have no network access, and the rustc in the Ubuntu
archive is older than this code needs, so the source package carries:

rustc / cargo / rust-std 1.97.1 (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu)
    The official standalone component tarballs from
    https://static.rust-lang.org/dist/, unmodified. debian/rules runs each
    one's install.sh into debian/.rust.

crates-<version>.tar.xz
    `cargo vendor --locked --versioned-dirs vendor` for this workspace, with
    every crate the Linux build of diskrescue, diskrescue-tui and
    diskrescue-gui does not use replaced by a stub (its Cargo.toml, an empty
    src/lib.rs and a .cargo-checksum.json with an empty file list but the
    original package checksum). Cargo still resolves the whole lockfile, but
    Windows/macOS/wasm-only crates and dev-dependencies are not shipped.

Regenerate both with packaging/vendor/make-vendor.sh whenever Cargo.lock or
the toolchain changes. SHA256SUMS lists all four files; debian/rules
verifies it before building. The tarballs are gitignored but included in the
source package.
